Attention working strategy to safely reset migrations

STEP 1 — Dump ONLY DATA (not schema)

On the production database dump everything:
!!!THIS RUNS ON THE PRODUCTION VM!!!
  docker compose -f docker-compose-prod.yaml exec -T -u postgres db pg_dump postgres > /tmp/myfaculty2026.data

STEP 2 — Drop & recreate the database

Create a test environment
!!!THIS RUNS ON THE DEV VM!!!
  sudo rm -r data
  docker compose up db
  docker compose exec -u postgres -T db psql postgres < myfaculty2026.data
  docker compose exec -u postgres -T pg_dump   --data-only   --column-inserts   --no-owner   --no-privileges   --disable-triggers   postgres > data.sql

STEP 3 — Drop the dev database again.
!!!THIS RUNS ON THE DEV VM!!!
  docker compose stop db
  sudo rm -r data
  
STEP 4 — Reset migrations in Django apps 
    !!!THIS RUNS ON THE DEV VM!!!
    sudo rm -r ./associates/migrations/0*.py
    sudo rm -r ./curricula/migrations/0*.py
    sudo rm -r ./leaves/migrations/0*.py
    sudo rm -r ./myprofile/migrations/0*.py
    sudo rm -r ./phdapplications/migrations/0*.py
    sudo rm -r ./projects/migrations/0*.py
    sudo rm -r ./theses/migrations/0*.py
    sudo rm -r ./timesheets/migrations/0*.p
   
STEP 5 — Recreate migrations from models
    !!!THIS RUNS ON THE DEV VM!!!
    docker compose up
    docker compose exec web python manage.py makemigrations
    docker compose exec web python manage.py migrate

STEP 6 — Reload the data
    !!!THIS RUNS ON THE DEV VM!!!
    docker compose exec -u postgres -T db psql postgres < data.sql
    

